  "body": "The mobile onboarding experiment client calls assignment/exposure endpoints absent from the current backend, despite the existing DTOs and migrated table. Restore the missing reviewed handlers from8c2960874, preserving the original migration and attribution, and keep the experiment explicitly paused. A progress-row lock and clock read after acquisition prevent completed/expired onboarding from being admitted during contention; account/version uniqueness and exposure compare-and-set retain idempotence.\n\nCanonical OpenAPI/web/mobile types are additive. Main4b0bc6ed7 is integrated, preserving notification APIs and migration ancestry. Deployment tooling forces and verifies the paused flag; no activation is part of this PR. No historical migration is rewritten.\n\nPre-integration validation: Stack9.10.3 --fast build;2578 backend examples,0failures,1PG-only pending; real HTTP/PostgreSQL tests with16concurrent assignments and16exposures, account isolation, paused no-write, completion/expiry lock contention and revocation;65release tests; full pinned TLC1.7.2/Alloy6.2.0 runner with three experiment negative controls. Native43conformance tests and TypeScript pass. Bounds and limits are recorded in the existing audit/formal records. Post-integration CI and generated mobile gitlink integration remain pending; draft until those gates finish. No deployment claimed.\n",
